{
  "strategy": "MAX LAND-GRAB 2137: unstick every 0-fuel hull with free warp-2 hops (Santa Maria #46 -> Kornephoros, Teamster #37 -> Shaula), launch fresh Santa Maria #58 at Epsilon Eridani, keep 5-6 distinct colonizer designs rolling at Shaula/Rasalhague/Gliese 1 behind mass mines, Teamsters reseed the dying rocks, research 0%.",
  "memo": "IRON FIST MEMO (2137). PHASE: MAX LAND-GRAB. 13 turns to the 2150 gate. WIN = 60 planets (only enabled target); tech/score disabled -> RESEARCH 0%. Own 32, panel reads 35. DESIGN CAP (21) IS FULL - submit NO new designs, they vanish silently.\nDEATH CLOCK (flat 100 colonists/yr regardless of pop): Betelgeuse 200 -> 2139, Zaurak 218 -> 2139, Kapteyn's 345 -> 2140, Groombridge 34 400 -> 2141, Deneb 500 -> 2142, Mimosa 1,000 -> 2147, Rana 1,200 -> 2149, Merak 2,400 safe, Sabik 5,900 safe. Each death = -1 planet. TERRAFORM CANNOT SAVE THEM: those rocks make 0 res/yr, so a queued Terraform never executes. Only Teamster reseeding works.\nRESEED GEOMETRY: Rasalhague (222,276) is 13 ly from Betelgeuse, 23 from Mimosa, 31 from Deneb - its Teamsters (70 kT = 7,000 colonists) land in 1-3 yrs and save three planets. Teamster #37 reaches Shaula 2138: load 7,000 there, it is 66 ly from Rana / 59 from Kapteyn's. Zaurak, Betelgeuse and Groombridge 34 are probably already lost. Teamster #40 (5,000 col) lands Rana 2144.\nFUEL LAW (fuel/ly = rate x mass / 3000): w1-2 rate 0 (FREE, 4 ly/yr), w3 = 20 (9 ly/yr), w4 = 60 (16 ly/yr), w5-6 = 100 (36 ly/yr). Spend <=85% of tank. A ship that empties mid-leg drops to WARP 0 forever - the engine does NOT coast. Every stranded hull gets a warp-2 order to the nearest useful star; NEVER issue warp 0. Gliese 1 starbase is the only refuel point.\nGERMANIUM, not resources, is the ship cap. Shaula has 529 res but 22 kT G surface, conc 17 -> its colonizers stall; queue 5 distinct ones anyway (the engine SKIPS unaffordable items instead of blocking) and pile mines behind them. NEVER factories at Shaula. Rasalhague (67 kT G, conc 53) and Gliese 1 are the real hull sources. Mines cost 0 minerals. Minerals are PER-PLANET.\nTHROUGHPUT LAW: quantity>1 at one star merges into one unsplittable fleet. Always quantity 1 with DISTINCT designs per star; the same design at a DIFFERENT star is fine. Max 6 queue items/star. Re-issue every yard queue yearly.\nEN ROUTE: Polaris (PF #54, lands 2138, hab 93%), Castor (SC #56, 2138), Sirius (SC #53, 2141), Cebalrai (PF #57, 2141), Epsilon Eridani (SM #58 launched 2137, lands 2143), Kornephoros (SM #46 crawling w2, hab 94%, 2147), Cursa (AP #47). Achernar landed.\nREMAINING TARGETS: Proxima, Ross 614, Wolf 1061, Kochab, Alnitak, Alcor, Elnath, Altair, Vega, Sadr, Sheliak, Ross 248, Barnard's Star. 33 stars unexplored - scouts crawl toward Bellatrix/Alioth/Sadr/Altair/Arcturus/Ross 248.\nMILITARY: e2 still shows ZERO armed hulls after 37 turns on 4 planets yet scores 409 to my 116. They mass Spore Clouds at Zubenelgenubi (328,154) - a colonisation race, not a war. Build no warships until an armed enemy hull is sighted; then Shaula pivots to Iron Fist (91 res, 350 armor).\nSTANDING RULES: 1. Reseed before you colonize. 2. Colonizers first, mines last, no factories at Shaula. 3. Load colonists the turn a hull launches. 4. Never warp 0, never quantity>1, never an empty queue. 5. Re-issue every queue yearly. 6. No new designs. 7. Colonize every rock, any hab.",
  "observations": [
    "Environmental colonist death is a FLAT 100/year independent of population: Merak (2,400 pop) and Betelgeuse (200 pop) both lose exactly 100/yr. Original Stars! kills a percentage of population, so a colony asymptotes rather than winking out. As implemented, any colony under ~1,000 pop on a negative-hab world is guaranteed to die in a handful of turns regardless of size, which makes small negative-hab colonies strictly unviable.",
    "Terraform is unreachable exactly where it is needed: negative-hab worlds produce 0 resources/yr, so a queued TERRAFORM never executes, and there is no way to ship resources to them. The only rescue path is freighting colonists in, which is a design dead end - the item sits in the queue forever with no message.",
    "Ships that exhaust fuel drop to warp 0 permanently and never coast or drift. Combined with no automatic refuelling outside a starbase, this permanently bricks fleets (Long Range Scout #1 and Stalwart Defender #1 have been emitting the same out-of-fuel message every turn since 2133). The repeated identical [Fuel] messages each year for already-stranded ships are also noise - the event should fire once on the transition, not every turn.",
    "The ship design slot cap (21) fails silently: submitting a new design past the cap returns no rejection and no message, the design simply never appears. Orders report 123 ok / 0 rejected even when a design submission was dropped.",
    "Score weighting looks badly skewed: e2 has 4 planets, 22 tech, 1571 resources and scores 409; I have 32 planets, 29 tech, 1536 resources and score 116. Planets owned appear to contribute almost nothing to score while population concentration dominates - eight times the territory yields a quarter of the score.",
    "Production quantity > 1 at a single star merges the output into one fleet that cannot be split, so N colony ships built together can only ever colonize one target. Workaround is one distinct design per queue slot, which collides with the 21-design cap and the 6-items-per-queue limit.",
    "Galactic storm damage (Shielded Scout #45) reports hull damage but no numeric value in the message, so there is no way to judge whether to flee or ride it out."
  ],
